{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/master/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "Trivy",
          "version": "0.69.0",
          "informationUri": "https://trivy.dev/",
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-45337",
              "name": "golang.org/x/crypto/ssh Vulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Potential authentication bypass in golang.org/x/crypto/ssh"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Applications and libraries which misuse the ServerConfig.PublicKeyCallback callback may be susceptible to an authorization bypass. The documentation for ServerConfig.PublicKeyCallback says thatichever key is selected by the callback, the KeyID field in the SSH certificate must be signed by that key. By exploiting the ServerConfig.PublicKeyCallback callback, an attacker may be able to authenticate using a different public key than the one originally intended."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-45337",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-45337\nSeverity: CRITICAL\nPackage: golang.org/x/crypto\nFixed Version: 0.31.0\nLink: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-45337",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-45337**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| CRITICAL | golang.org/x/crypto | 0.31.0 |\n\n[More Info](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-45337)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "9.1",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "CRITICAL",
                  "CWE-287",
                  "go",
                  "supply-chain"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-45338",
              "name": "golang.org/x/net/html Vulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Denial of Service in golang.org/x/net/html parsing"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An attacker can craft an input to the Parse functions that would be processed non-linearly with respect to its length, resulting in extremely long parsing times. This could cause a denial of service when parsing HTML content from untrusted sources."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-45338",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-45338\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: golang.org/x/net\nFixed Version: 0.33.0\nLink: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-45338",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-45338**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| HIGH | golang.org/x/net | 0.33.0 |\n\n[More Info](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-45338)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH",
                  "CWE-400",
                  "go",
                  "supply-chain"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-45336",
              "name": "Standard Library HTTP Request Vulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "HTTP request handling vulnerability in Go standard library"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The HTTP client drops sensitive headers after a redirect to a different host. When an HTTP redirect to a different host occurs, the Authorization header and other sensitive headers are stripped from the redirected request. A maliciously crafted HTTP redirect may cause sensitive headers to be unexpectedly forwarded."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-45336",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-45336\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.22.10\nLink: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-45336",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-45336**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| MEDIUM | stdlib | 1.22.10 |\n\n[More Info](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-45336)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "6.1",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM",
                  "CWE-200",
                  "go",
                  "stdlib"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-24791",
              "name": "net/http HTTP/2 Protocol Vulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Denial of Service via HTTP/2 CONTINUATION frames"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The net/http HTTP/1.1 client mishandled the case where a server responds to a request with an HTTP status code 1xx, which causes subsequent requests sent on that connection to be treated as 1xx responses. This could allow a malicious server to cause excessive resource consumption on the client."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-24791",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-24791\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.21.12, 1.22.5\nLink: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-24791",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-24791**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| HIGH | stdlib | 1.21.12, 1.22.5 |\n\n[More Info](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-24791)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH",
                  "CWE-400",
                  "go",
                  "stdlib"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-34158",
              "name": "go/build/constraint Parsing Vulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Stack exhaustion in go/build/constraint parsing"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Calling Parse on a 'build constraint' line containing deeply nested expressions can cause a stack exhaustion, leading to a denial of service. Build constraints are used by the Go toolchain to selectively include or exclude files during the build process."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-34158",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-34158\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.22.7, 1.23.1\nLink: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-34158",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-34158**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| HIGH | stdlib | 1.22.7, 1.23.1 |\n\n[More Info](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-34158)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH",
                  "CWE-674",
                  "go",
                  "stdlib"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-34155",
              "name": "go/parser Parsing Vulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Stack exhaustion in go/parser"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Calling any of the Parse functions on Go source code which contains deeply nested literals can cause a panic due to stack exhaustion. This affects parsing of Go source files and expressions."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-34155",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-34155\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.22.7, 1.23.1\nLink: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-34155",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-34155**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| HIGH | stdlib | 1.22.7, 1.23.1 |\n\n[More Info](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-34155)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
