                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-48795",
              "name": "golang.org/x/crypto/ssh Terrapin Attack",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "SSH Terrapin attack prefix truncation vulnerability"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The SSH transport protocol with certain OpenSSH extensions allows remote attackers to bypass integrity checks such that some packets are omitted from the extension negotiation message. This is known as the Terrapin attack and affects messages using ChaCha20-Poly1305 or CBC with Encrypt-then-MAC."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-48795",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-48795\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: golang.org/x/crypto\nFixed Version: 0.17.0\nLink: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-48795",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-48795**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| MEDIUM | golang.org/x/crypto | 0.17.0 |\n\n[More Info](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-48795)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.9",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM",
                  "CWE-354",
                  "go",
                  "supply-chain"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-47108",
              "name": "OpenTelemetry gRPC DoS Vulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Denial of Service in OpenTelemetry-Go Contrib gRPC handler"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The grpc instrumentation in opentelemetry-go-contrib has a memory leak bug that occurs when processing very large payloads. A malicious client can send large payloads which will exhaust the server's memory and cause a denial of service."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-47108",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-47108\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: go.opentelemetry.io/contrib/instrumentation/google.golang.org/grpc/otelgrpc\nFixed Version: 0.46.0\nLink: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-47108",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-47108**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| HIGH | go.opentelemetry.io/contrib/instrumentation/google.golang.org/grpc/otelgrpc | 0.46.0 |\n\n[More Info](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-47108)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH",
                  "CWE-770",
                  "go",
                  "supply-chain"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "TRIVY-MISCONFIG-K8S-0001",
              "name": "Kubernetes Privileged Container",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Container running with privileged security context"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A container is running in privileged mode. Privileged containers have all of the root capabilities of the host machine, allowing potential container escape and unauthorized access to host resources."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/security/pod-security-standards/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration TRIVY-MISCONFIG-K8S-0001\nSeverity: HIGH\nType: Kubernetes\nCheck: Privileged Container\n\nRemediation: Set securityContext.privileged to false",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration TRIVY-MISCONFIG-K8S-0001**\n| Severity | Type | Check |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| HIGH | Kubernetes | Privileged Container |\n\n**Remediation:** Set `securityContext.privileged` to `false`"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "kubernetes",
                  "HIGH",
                  "CWE-250",
                  "container-security"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "TRIVY-MISCONFIG-K8S-0002",
              "name": "Kubernetes hostNetwork Enabled",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Pod configured with hostNetwork: true"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The pod specification includes hostNetwork: true, which allows the pod to share the host's network namespace. This can lead to network privilege escalation and bypass of network policies."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/security/pod-security-standards/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration TRIVY-MISCONFIG-K8S-0002\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nType: Kubernetes\nCheck: hostNetwork Enabled\n\nRemediation: Remove hostNetwork: true unless absolutely required",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration TRIVY-MISCONFIG-K8S-0002**\n| Severity | Type | Check |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| MEDIUM | Kubernetes | hostNetwork Enabled |\n\n**Remediation:** Remove `hostNetwork: true` unless absolutely required"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "6.5",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "kubernetes",
                  "MEDIUM",
                  "CWE-284",
                  "container-security"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "TRIVY-MISCONFIG-K8S-0003",
              "name": "Kubernetes hostPath Volume Mount",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Container mounting sensitive host path"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The container is configured to mount a hostPath volume which can expose sensitive host files and directories to the container, potentially allowing container escape or data exfiltration."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/storage/volumes/#hostpath",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration TRIVY-MISCONFIG-K8S-0003\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nType: Kubernetes\nCheck: hostPath Volume Mount\n\nRemediation: Use emptyDir or PersistentVolumeClaim instead of hostPath",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration TRIVY-MISCONFIG-K8S-0003**\n| Severity | Type | Check |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| MEDIUM | Kubernetes | hostPath Volume Mount |\n\n**Remediation:** Use `emptyDir` or `PersistentVolumeClaim` instead of `hostPath`"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "6.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "kubernetes",
                  "MEDIUM",
                  "CWE-668",
                  "container-security"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "TRIVY-MISCONFIG-K8S-0004",
              "name": "Kubernetes Missing Resource Limits",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Container without resource limits defined"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The container does not have resource limits defined. Without limits, a container can consume all available resources on the node, potentially causing denial of service for other workloads."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/configuration/manage-resources-containers/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration TRIVY-MISCONFIG-K8S-0004\nSeverity: LOW\nType: Kubernetes\nCheck: Missing Resource Limits\n\nRemediation: Set resources.limits.cpu and resources.limits.memory",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration TRIVY-MISCONFIG-K8S-0004**\n| Severity | Type | Check |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| LOW | Kubernetes | Missing Resource Limits |\n\n**Remediation:** Set `resources.limits.cpu` and `resources.limits.memory`"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "3.5",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "kubernetes",
                  "LOW",
                  "CWE-400",
                  "resource-management"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "TRIVY-MISCONFIG-K8S-0005",
              "name": "Kubernetes ClusterRole with Wildcard Permissions",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "ClusterRole with overly permissive wildcard rules"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The ClusterRole contains rules with wildcard (*) permissions on resources or verbs. This grants excessive permissions and violates the principle of least privilege."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/rbac/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration TRIVY-MISCONFIG-K8S-0005\nSeverity: HIGH\nType: Kubernetes\nCheck: ClusterRole with Wildcard Permissions\n\nRemediation: Replace wildcard (*) with specific resource names and verbs",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration TRIVY-MISCONFIG-K8S-0005**\n| Severity | Type | Check |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| HIGH | Kubernetes | ClusterRole with Wildcard Permissions |\n\n**Remediation:** Replace wildcard (`*`) with specific resource names and verbs"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "kubernetes",
                  "HIGH",
                  "CWE-732",
                  "rbac"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "TRIVY-MISCONFIG-K8S-0006",
              "name": "Kubernetes Missing Security Context",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Container without security context defined"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The container specification does not include a security context. Without explicit security context settings, containers may run with elevated privileges by default."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/configure-pod-container/security-context/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration TRIVY-MISCONFIG-K8S-0006\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nType: Kubernetes\nCheck: Missing Security Context\n\nRemediation: Add securityContext with runAsNonRoot: true and readOnlyRootFilesystem: true",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration TRIVY-MISCONFIG-K8S-0006**\n| Severity | Type | Check |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| MEDIUM | Kubernetes | Missing Security Context |\n\n**Remediation:** Add `securityContext` with `runAsNonRoot: true` and `readOnlyRootFilesystem: true`"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "kubernetes",
                  "MEDIUM",
                  "CWE-250",
                  "container-security"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "TRIVY-MISCONFIG-K8S-0007",
              "name": "Kubernetes NET_ADMIN Capability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Container with NET_ADMIN capability"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The container is configured with NET_ADMIN capability which allows network administration operations. This can be used to modify network settings and potentially intercept or redirect network traffic."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/configure-pod-container/security-context/#set-capabilities-for-a-container",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration TRIVY-MISCONFIG-K8S-0007\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nType: Kubernetes\nCheck: NET_ADMIN Capability\n\nRemediation: Remove NET_ADMIN from capabilities.add unless strictly required",
