            {
              "id": "TRIVY-MISCONFIG-DOCKER-0001",
              "name": "Dockerfile Running as Root",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Container runs as root user by default"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The Dockerfile does not specify a non-root USER instruction. Containers running as root have elevated privileges and can lead to security vulnerabilities if the container is compromised."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/#user",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration TRIVY-MISCONFIG-DOCKER-0001\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nType: Dockerfile\nCheck: Running as Root\n\nRemediation: Add USER instruction with non-root user before CMD/ENTRYPOINT",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration TRIVY-MISCONFIG-DOCKER-0001**\n| Severity | Type | Check |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| MEDIUM | Dockerfile | Running as Root |\n\n**Remediation:** Add `USER` instruction with non-root user before `CMD`/`ENTRYPOINT`"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "dockerfile",
                  "MEDIUM",
                  "CWE-250",
                  "container-security"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "TRIVY-MISCONFIG-DOCKER-0002",
              "name": "Dockerfile Using Latest Tag",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Base image using 'latest' tag or no tag"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The Dockerfile uses a base image with the 'latest' tag or no tag specified. This can lead to non-reproducible builds and unexpected security vulnerabilities when the base image is updated."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/#from",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration TRIVY-MISCONFIG-DOCKER-0002\nSeverity: LOW\nType: Dockerfile\nCheck: Using Latest Tag\n\nRemediation: Pin base image to specific version tag or digest",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration TRIVY-MISCONFIG-DOCKER-0002**\n| Severity | Type | Check |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| LOW | Dockerfile | Using Latest Tag |\n\n**Remediation:** Pin base image to specific version tag or digest"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "dockerfile",
                  "LOW",
                  "CWE-829",
                  "supply-chain"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "TRIVY-MISCONFIG-DOCKER-0003",
              "name": "Dockerfile ADD Instead of COPY",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Using ADD instruction instead of COPY"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The Dockerfile uses ADD instruction which has auto-extraction behavior and can fetch remote URLs. COPY should be preferred for simple file copying as it is more predictable and secure."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/#add",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration TRIVY-MISCONFIG-DOCKER-0003\nSeverity: LOW\nType: Dockerfile\nCheck: ADD Instead of COPY\n\nRemediation: Use COPY instead of ADD unless auto-extraction is required",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration TRIVY-MISCONFIG-DOCKER-0003**\n| Severity | Type | Check |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| LOW | Dockerfile | ADD Instead of COPY |\n\n**Remediation:** Use `COPY` instead of `ADD` unless auto-extraction is required"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "medium",
                "security-severity": "2.5",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "dockerfile",
                  "LOW",
                  "CWE-829",
                  "best-practice"
                ]
              }
            },
